WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.110 --> 00:00:05.549
Hey Team it’s Charlie thanks to everyone
who submitted questions for this week’s

00:00:05.549 --> 00:00:06.549
Q&amp;A.

00:00:06.549 --> 00:00:10.249
I saw a lot of you were wondering the same
thing about secret identities and people coming

00:00:10.249 --> 00:00:11.249
back for the finale.

00:00:11.249 --> 00:00:15.156
I also have some announcements about next
week I’ll make at the end of the video just

00:00:15.156 --> 00:00:17.280
because some new stuff is coming next week.

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:21.010
I’m also going to start including more of
that in the video descriptions below.

00:00:21.010 --> 00:00:23.000
So be sure to check there.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:26.180
This episode was the last of the leaked scripts
too, so I think we’ll be able to have a

00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:29.790
little more fun talking about what we think
is going to happen even though there were

00:00:29.790 --> 00:00:31.730
still a few leaked pictures from the finale.

00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:34.980
Speaking of which Time Heist, careful for
spoilers from the episode if you haven’t

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:35.980
seen it yet.

00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:38.180
I’ll wait just a sec...okay here we go

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:42.520
Question 1 - Jack Marriot asks when is The
Doctor going to start talking about where

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:44.360
his face came from again?

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:49.440
It’s possible they could wait till the last
couple of episodes.

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:52.149
I think there’s two things going on here.

00:00:52.149 --> 00:00:56.350
I think it’s a clever way to reference Capaldi’s
other characters from Doctor Who and Torchwood

00:00:56.350 --> 00:01:00.180
and I think it’s going to tie in with the
finale.

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:03.820
Because of the way these episodes are mostly
one-offs and don’t really carry over too

00:01:03.820 --> 00:01:08.830
much, I’m thinking more and more that they’ll
wait till the end of the season to directly

00:01:08.830 --> 00:01:12.040
address it.

00:01:12.040 --> 00:01:14.280
Use a giant chunk of an episode to talk about
it.

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:18.330
He did make the joke about coming out looking
like a Magician, so at least he’s referencing

00:01:18.330 --> 00:01:19.330
himself.

00:01:19.330 --> 00:01:21.280
I think we’ll see more of that in the one-off
episodes.

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:22.510
Him just making fun of himself.

00:01:22.510 --> 00:01:26.000
But I don’t know that’s necessarily part
of the overarching plot.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:28.820
I think it’s just the writers being cheeky.

00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:33.140
Question 2 - Blue Headphones asks At the end
when the Doctor jokes about the date, do you

00:01:33.140 --> 00:01:36.160
think the Doctor and Danny will compete over
Clara?

00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:41.840
I really hope not, I do think they’ll address
it next week in Episode 6.

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:43.950
It looks like Clara is as tired as I am.

00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:47.600
Right now she’s burning the candle at both
ends, spending all the extra time with The

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:57.320
Doctor and returning to her normal life as
if no time has passed at all.

00:01:57.320 --> 00:02:05.070
Theoretically, if a companion wanted to.

00:02:05.070 --> 00:02:07.110
They could stay with the Doctor their entire
life.

00:02:07.110 --> 00:02:11.000
So even though they always return to the point
they left off, they still age normally.

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:14.760
Meaning that unless Clara is sleeping on the
TARDIS, she’s probably not sleeping much

00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:15.910
at all.

00:02:15.910 --> 00:02:31.030
I liked the Doctor’s joke about calories
consumed on the TARDIS, it’s the same thing

00:02:31.030 --> 00:02:32.850
with sleep.

00:02:32.850 --> 00:02:37.560
Question 3 - wofllover asks do you think the
other characters Capaldi has played on Doctor

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:38.880
Who and Torchwood were clones?

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:43.100
I don’t, but back when Russell Davies was
still doing Torchwood and he cast Capaldi

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:44.130
he came up with a clever explanation.

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:47.209
I don’t think he ever said what it was,
but he did plan to address it.

00:02:47.209 --> 00:02:51.310
Obviously Moffat has since cast him as The
Doctor, negating whatever Davies story would

00:02:51.310 --> 00:02:54.700
have been but I’m sure he also has his own
explanation.

00:02:54.700 --> 00:02:57.730
In Deep Breath he said he felt like he was
trying to tell himself something.

00:02:57.730 --> 00:03:02.099
I don’t think those other faces will be
critical to that, I think the explanation

00:03:02.099 --> 00:03:03.819
will be less complex.

00:03:03.819 --> 00:03:08.640
But for fans of Torchwood and the big whovians
I think Moffat’s explanation will allow

00:03:08.640 --> 00:03:11.540
room for tin foil hat theories.

00:03:11.540 --> 00:03:15.349
A lot of times when fans confront Moffat with
big questions about plot holes his answers

00:03:15.349 --> 00:03:19.340
make it sound like he wants there to be multiple
interpretations.

00:03:19.340 --> 00:03:26.530
I do think we’ll learn what The Doctor’s
face means by the finale, but I think it will

00:03:26.530 --> 00:03:28.159
satisfy everyone’s questions.

00:03:28.159 --> 00:03:31.630
Think about it this way, there are still people
debating how many new regnerations The Doctor

00:03:31.630 --> 00:03:32.630
was given in the christmas special.

00:03:32.630 --> 00:03:39.379
And Moffat has never gone on record stating
a number.

00:03:39.379 --> 00:03:43.990
Question 4 - Joe Kerr asks do you think we’ll
see River Song anytime soon?

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:47.670
I’m kind of hoping we don’t but not because
I hate her or anything.

00:03:47.670 --> 00:03:51.620
What I’d really like to see is a big twist
in the finale that doesn’t completely depend

00:03:51.620 --> 00:03:53.750
on something from a previous series.

00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:57.300
I really like the idea of them doing something
fresh.

00:03:57.300 --> 00:03:59.550
Like Missy not having anything to do with
River.

00:03:59.550 --> 00:04:01.239
Just being someone totally new.

00:04:01.239 --> 00:04:03.739
The woman in the shop with the Doctor’s
phone number is a good example.

00:04:03.739 --> 00:04:08.080
I’d be a little disappointed if it was River
this whole time.

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:12.220
I feel like with the exception of new people
we’ll meet between now and the finale.

00:04:12.220 --> 00:04:18.339
We’ve already met all the people that will
be critical to the big arcs in series 8.

00:04:18.339 --> 00:04:23.759
Even if there’s a big Moffat Loop at the
end.

00:04:23.759 --> 00:04:27.490
I still like the idea that someone could start
watching the show for the first time this

00:04:27.490 --> 00:04:32.599
year with Deep Breath, watch only the Series
8 episodes and be able to understand who all

00:04:32.599 --> 00:04:38.339
the characters are and the big twist in the
finale.

00:04:38.339 --> 00:04:45.080
That just feels like a much cleaner execution
from a storytelling perspective.

00:04:45.080 --> 00:04:50.129
It feels like something the BBC would be happier
with from an audience development standpoint

00:04:50.129 --> 00:04:51.129
too.

00:04:51.129 --> 00:04:55.689
It would be too daunting to new viewers if
they had to do a mountain of homework just

00:04:55.689 --> 00:05:05.610
to understand what’s going on.

00:05:05.610 --> 00:05:09.270
Question 5 - David Rice asks what do you think
happened to all the regular people in the

00:05:09.270 --> 00:05:12.589
bank when the solar storm destroyed the planet?

00:05:12.589 --> 00:05:16.460
Part of me wants to think they were all killed,
or at least the ones not deep inside the earth.

00:05:16.460 --> 00:05:23.180
The strange thing is if they were in the far
future and had all that cool security technology,

00:05:23.180 --> 00:05:26.770
would they also be able to forecast solar
weather.

00:05:26.770 --> 00:05:33.500
It seemed like the Solar Storm was a big surprise,
but if they had such advanced tech, why didn’t

00:05:33.500 --> 00:05:35.800
they know it was going to happen?

00:05:35.800 --> 00:05:40.360
Big events like that still take a while to
happen, it’s not instantaneous.

00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:48.020
So we’ll just call that a plot hole.

00:05:48.020 --> 00:05:52.219
Question 6 - Orlando asks Do you think that
Psi and Saibra will have anything to do with

00:05:52.219 --> 00:05:53.720
the finale?

00:05:53.720 --> 00:05:57.740
The finale talks about old friends and old
enemies manouvering around The Doctor, so

00:05:57.740 --> 00:05:59.129
it’s possible.

00:05:59.129 --> 00:06:04.679
When I think about Saibra’s powers, they
feel a lot like the Tesselecta, with the ability

00:06:04.679 --> 00:06:08.789
to mimick other people and that was the solution
to the series 6 plot.

00:06:08.789 --> 00:06:12.879
So part of me feels like they wouldn’t use
that again.

00:06:12.879 --> 00:06:17.409
I believe that the patternoster gang is rumored
to be back and the UNIT characters, but aside

00:06:17.409 --> 00:06:22.749
from them I haven’t seen any news about
other friendly characters.

00:06:22.749 --> 00:06:27.210
Question 7 - Sarah Walden asks Do you think
they’d kill Clara off if she leaves this

00:06:27.210 --> 00:06:33.339
year? or Go more Amy and Rory with it?

00:06:33.339 --> 00:06:35.490
I don’t think it would grotesque or anything.

00:06:35.490 --> 00:06:38.440
I guess I am expecting an Amy Rory ending.

00:06:38.440 --> 00:06:39.559
Not the exact same thing.

00:06:39.559 --> 00:06:44.120
But I feel like she’d pay a big price and
still get a happy ending with Danny Pink.

00:06:44.120 --> 00:06:49.740
It feels like the show is pushing her towards
Danny Pink and wants us to feel like it’s

00:06:49.740 --> 00:06:50.740
a good thing.

00:06:50.740 --> 00:06:53.050
Regardless of what might happen to him in
the finale.

00:06:53.050 --> 00:06:54.849
I think he’s a good character.

00:06:54.849 --> 00:06:57.099
It is moffat, so I think she won’t walk
away completely intact.

00:06:57.099 --> 00:07:00.330
I don’t think it will be straight up Dalek
Oswin, but something close.

00:07:00.330 --> 00:07:05.059
That’s only if she does go, there is a small
chance she’ll stay on.

00:07:05.059 --> 00:07:09.589
But it feels like the show is preparing us
for her to leave.

00:07:09.589 --> 00:07:12.309
Mostly with all this Danny Pink romance stuff.

00:07:12.309 --> 00:07:16.229
Question 8 - Micki Chiba asks do you think
lady karabraxos is Romana?

00:07:16.229 --> 00:07:18.479
I think she was a completely new character.

00:07:18.479 --> 00:07:21.080
That’s what the BBC called her.

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:22.080
A new villain.

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:26.330
It’s possible she could come back as a clone
but I’m thinking more and more with each

00:07:26.330 --> 00:07:39.959
episode, that none of the characters is secretly
someone from classic who.

00:07:39.959 --> 00:07:45.009
Question 9 - fg pinkey asks What was Clara’s
reward for robbing the bank?

00:07:45.009 --> 00:07:49.800
Good question, I think it was just the date.

00:07:49.800 --> 00:07:51.009
As the Doctor called it.

00:07:51.009 --> 00:07:54.189
Getting the thrill of robbing the richest
bank in the Universe.

00:07:54.189 --> 00:07:59.689
The doctor made that comment that he didn’t
know what his reward was and I think his also

00:07:59.689 --> 00:08:02.129
might have been tied to that idea of the date.

00:08:02.129 --> 00:08:08.149
Like he was rewarded with the thrill of seeing
Clara get a thrill.

00:08:08.149 --> 00:08:11.949
Even though they did that big speech in Deep
Breath about the doctor no longer seeking

00:08:11.949 --> 00:08:16.199
approval of others through his appearance.

00:08:16.199 --> 00:08:27.869
It still feels like he wants approval from
Clara if he’s still trying to impress her.

00:08:27.869 --> 00:08:31.889
